\details{
Implements the correct BLUP prediction error variance formula from Henderson (1984):
PEV = σ²ᵤ[G₂₂ - G₂₁V₁₁⁻¹G₁₂ - G₂₁V₁₁⁻¹X₁(X₁'V₁₁⁻¹X₁)⁻¹X₁'V₁₁⁻¹G₁₂]

where V₁₁ = σ²ᵤG₁₁ + σ²ₑI and both correction terms are SUBTRACTED.

This function implements BLUP (Best Linear Unbiased Prediction) theory for
mixed models with heritability h² = σ²ᵤ/(σ²ᵤ + σ²ₑ).

For mixed model y = Xβ + Zu + e where u ~ N(0, σ²ᵤG) and e ~ N(0, σ²ₑI),
the BLUP PEV is:
PEV = σ²ᵤ[G₂₂ - G₂₁V₁₁⁻¹G₁₂ - G₂₁V₁₁⁻¹X₁C⁻¹X₁'V₁₁⁻¹G₁₂]
where V₁₁ = σ²ᵤG₁₁ + σ²ₑI = (σ²ᵤ + σ²ₑ)[h²G₁₁ + (1-h²)I]

The PEV can be normalized by total variance (σ²ᵤ + σ²ₑ) to get a scale-free measure.
